[] How do I deal with Wraiths without getting seriously drained ?

umm, missile attacks before they get close.  or how about bashing
them with a clove of garlic (try it)?  in hand-to-ethereal-hand
combat you might want a double-digit negative AC rating.  also, as
you state below, Excalibur would be quite handy (it makes a difference,
as does Stormbringer).  perhaps the best defense is a good offense
(since you get the first move).  finally, wraiths respect `Elbereth',
so spread the word when you're in trouble ...

[] Finally, why do I never get weapons when I sacrifice any more ?
[] I've got Sunsword and Werebane, but that's it. Now everytime I
[] offer something, even quite big corpses, I get a four leaved clover
[] at my feet. Luck is nice, but excalibur would be quite handy, too.

damage-wise Excalibur isn't as good (statistically) as Sunsword or
Werebane (all things being equal).  when the conditions are right
the weapons fall randomly.  if the weapon already exists you won't
get a duplicate by this method (or any other method presumably).
holding out for Mjollnir may be worth the effort but you can
get Excalibur by other (more common) means ...

